Subject: [PATCH 01139/11171] =?UTF-8?q?[outer-loop]=20Route=20exp4008=20ar?=
 =?UTF-8?q?chive=20task=20to=20claude/Opus=20(requires=5Fclaude=5Fverified?=
 =?UTF-8?q?)=20=E2=80=94=20it=20hit=20the=20codex=2080-min=20wall-clock=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?cap=202x?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The .371 archive/activate task is the textbook multi-file-choreography case the
planner correctly marked agent_type:claude — but Codex-Default v2 coerced it to
codex, where gpt-5.5 looped past the 80-min HARD wall-clock cap twice (15:09
4027s, 16:33 4801s) without emitting the artifact. Its deliverables already
exist and its test passes 29/29; the agent call just can't close out under the
cap. requires_claude_verified:true is the operator-only bypass for exactly this
('codex keeps failing a genuine multi-file task'); claude has STALL_TIMEOUT=0.
Conductor restarted (also activates the IDLE_GRACE 300->600 fix from 7142c7eac).
Surgical 6-line YAML edit (header comments preserved).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
